[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi, I'm reviewing the \"SAFETY:TODO\" in rust/kernel/list module, and I found that there is a \"SAFETY: TODO\" in the implementation of <code>impl_has_list_links_self_ptr</code> macro:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/// Implements the [`HasListLinks`] and [`HasSelfPtr`] traits for the given type.</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#[macro_export]</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#[doc(hidden)]</span>\n<span class=\"fm\">macro_rules!</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">impl_has_list_links_self_ptr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"cp\">$(</span><span class=\"k\">impl</span><span class=\"cp\">$(</span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"cp\">$($generics</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"nc\">tt</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"p\">})</span><span class=\"o\">?</span>\n<span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"n\">HasSelfPtr</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"cp\">$item_type</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"nc\">ty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$(,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$id</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"nc\">tt</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">?&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$self</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"nc\">ty</span>\n<span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"cp\">$(</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"cp\">$field</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"nc\">ident</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"cp\">$(</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"c1\">// SAFETY: The implementation of `raw_get_list_links` only compiles if the field has the</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"c1\">// right type.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">unsafe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">impl</span><span class=\"cp\">$(</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"cp\">$($generics</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">*&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$crate</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">HasSelfPtr</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"cp\">$item_type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$(,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$id</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">?&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$self</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"c1\">// SAFETY: TODO.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">unsafe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">impl</span><span class=\"cp\">$(</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"cp\">$($generics</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">*&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$crate</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">HasListLinks</span><span class=\"cp\">$(</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"cp\">$id</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$self</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"cp\">#[inline]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"k\">unsafe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">raw_get_list_links</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ptr</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"k\">mut</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">Self</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"k\">mut</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$crate</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">ListLinks</span><span class=\"cp\">$(</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"cp\">$id</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"kd\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ptr</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"k\">mut</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$crate</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">ListLinksSelfPtr</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"cp\">$item_type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$(,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$id</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">?&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                    </span><span class=\"c1\">// SAFETY: The caller promises that the pointer is not dangling.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                    </span><span class=\"k\">unsafe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">ptr</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">addr_of_mut</span><span class=\"o\">!</span><span class=\"p\">((</span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"n\">ptr</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"cp\">$(</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"cp\">$field</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">};</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"n\">ptr</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cast</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"p\">};</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I found that the implementation detail of <code>raw_get_list_links</code> is different from the implementation of <code>impl_has_list_links</code> macro. The difference is in <code>impl_has_list_links</code> it implement <code>raw_get_list_links</code> by adding <code>offset_of!</code> macro to check the field is directly within the <code>Self</code> allocation(not using Box, for example):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/// Implements the [`HasListLinks`] trait for the given type.</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#[macro_export]</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#[doc(hidden)]</span>\n<span class=\"fm\">macro_rules!</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">impl_has_list_links</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"cp\">$(</span><span class=\"k\">impl</span><span class=\"cp\">$(</span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"cp\">$($generics</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"nc\">tt</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"p\">})</span><span class=\"o\">?</span>\n<span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"n\">HasListLinks</span><span class=\"cp\">$(</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"cp\">$id</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"nc\">tt</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">?</span>\n<span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$self</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"nc\">ty</span>\n<span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"cp\">$(</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"cp\">$field</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"nc\">ident</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"cp\">$(</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"c1\">// SAFETY: The implementation of `raw_get_list_links` only compiles if the field has the</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"c1\">// right type.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">unsafe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">impl</span><span class=\"cp\">$(</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"cp\">$($generics</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">*&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$crate</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">HasListLinks</span><span class=\"cp\">$(</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"cp\">$id</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$self</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"cp\">#[inline]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"k\">unsafe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">raw_get_list_links</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ptr</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"k\">mut</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">Self</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"k\">mut</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$crate</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">ListLinks</span><span class=\"cp\">$(</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"cp\">$id</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"c1\">// Statically ensure that `$(.field)*` doesn't follow any pointers.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"c1\">//</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"c1\">// Cannot be `const` because `$self` may contain generics and E0401 says constants</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"c1\">// \"can't use {`Self`,generic parameters} from outer item\".</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">usize</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">mem</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">offset_of</span><span class=\"o\">!</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">Self</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$($field</span><span class=\"p\">).</span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"c1\">// SAFETY: The caller promises that the pointer is not dangling. We know that this</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"c1\">// expression doesn't follow any pointers, as the `offset_of!` invocation above</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"c1\">// would otherwise not compile.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"k\">unsafe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">ptr</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">addr_of_mut</span><span class=\"o\">!</span><span class=\"p\">((</span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"n\">ptr</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"cp\">$(</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"cp\">$field</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"p\">};</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>So why <code>impl_has_list_links_self_ptr!</code> doesn't add <code>offset_of!</code> macro to perform the same check? I understand that the <code>ListLinksSelfPtr</code> implementation use <code>addr_of!</code> to recover <code>Self</code> directly (Because of DST we need to get complete pointer). But now it allows <code>`ListLinksSelfPtr</code> to be in some other allocation but not in <code>Self</code>.</p>",
